            <ArticleTitle>Left main coronary artery dissection during percutaneous coronary intervention in patient with chronic total occlusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Catheter induced left main coronary artery dissection is a rare but well recognized life threatening complication of coronary angiography and angioplasty. We present a case of left main coronary artery dissection induced with a guide catheter while dealing with chronic total occlusion (CTO) and bailout stenting of left main and Left anterior descending (LAD) artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
